          %h2#definition Definition
          #SubspaceTopology.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"}> subspace topology
                )
            %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/OpenSubsetsOfSquareInsidePlane.png", :width => "200"}/
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \tau_X)
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \subset X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
              of its underlying
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              has
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              as its underlying set, and its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              are those subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              which arise as restrictions of open subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              (i.e.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
              of open subsets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              = succeed "):" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi Y
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Y
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mtext open
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ∃
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi X
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi τ
                            %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi Y
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi X
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi Y
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    U_Y \subset Y\,\,\text{open}
                    \\right)
                    \\,\Leftrightarrow\,
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{U_X \in \tau_X}{\exists} \left( U_Y = U_X \cap Y \right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              In other words,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi τ
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau_Y
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finer+topology"} smallest topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              such that the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \hookrightarrow X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+topology"} initial topology
              on that map).
            %p
              The picture on the right shows two open subsets inside the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square"} square
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            %blockquote
              %p
                graphics grabbed from
                %a{:href => "#Munkres75"} Munkres 75
          %p
            The pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi τ
                    %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,\tau_Y)
            is then said to be a
            %em
              topological
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace"} subspace
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
